# Cal.com: Scheduling Infrastructure for Individuals, Teams, and Organizations


> Cal.com is a scheduling platform and scheduling API for individuals, teams, and organizations. Share a booking link, connect your calendars, and let people pick a time without the back-and-forth. It powers one-on-one, group, round-robin, and collective scheduling, with routing forms, workflows, payments, native video, and an app store of integrations. The commercial product is closed source with a generous free tier and per-seat paid plans; the MIT-licensed, self-hostable community edition is a separate project called Cal.diy.


**Key Terms**: Scheduling Software, Appointment Scheduling, Booking Link, Calendar Management, Meeting Scheduler, Round-Robin Routing, Collective Scheduling, Group Events, Routing Forms, Workflows, Scheduling API, Embeddable Scheduling, Cal Atoms, Cal Video, HIPAA-Compliant Scheduling, SOC 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, CCPA, SSO/SAML, SCIM, RBAC, Audit Logs, Calendly Alternative, Open-Source Scheduling (Cal.diy), MCP Server, AI Scheduling Agents.


