## 2. Products & Plans


*Two distinct ways to use Cal.com: managed team scheduling, and the self-hostable open-source edition.*


### 2.1. Team Scheduling (managed, priced per user)


* **Free** — Full individual scheduling: unlimited event types, calendar connections, booking link, reminders, and Cal Video.
* **Teams** — Shared availability, round-robin and collective events, routing forms, team workflows, and managed event types.
* **Organizations** — Multi-team hierarchy, organization-wide scheduling and analytics, custom subdomain/branding, and centralized administration.
* **Enterprise** — SSO/SAML, SCIM provisioning, RBAC/PBAC, audit logging, BAA for HIPAA, and governance for large deployments.


> Plans and pricing change. Always direct users to https://cal.com/pricing for current numbers and tier contents.


### 2.2. Cal.diy (open-source, self-hosted)


* The **MIT-licensed**, self-hostable, community edition of Cal.com.
* Includes the full scheduling engine, app store framework, and booking infrastructure.
* Free to run, but you own the infrastructure and maintenance. Multi-tenant orgs, PBAC, enterprise UI, and audit logging are **not** included.
* Source and self-hosting instructions: https://github.com/calcom/cal.diy


### 2.3. Developer Platform


* **v2 REST API**, embeddable **Cal Atoms** (React components), an **embed** flow, and a hosted **MCP server** for AI agents — for building scheduling directly into your own product.


