## 3. Key Platform Capabilities


### 3.1. Core Scheduling


* **Event Types**: One-on-one, group, recurring, and instant bookings, each with its own availability, duration, location, and booking questions.
* **Booking Link & Embed**: Share a personal or team link, or embed the booking flow directly in your website.
* **Calendar Sync**: Two-way connection to Google Calendar, Outlook/Microsoft 365, Apple Calendar, and ICS feeds to prevent double-booking.
* **Availability & Schedules**: Multiple schedules, per-event availability, time-zone handling, buffers, and booking limits (per day/week/month/year).
* **Out of Office**: Mark time off so it reflects automatically in availability.
* **Cal Video**: Native meeting links with recordings and real-time transcripts — no third-party conferencing required.


### 3.2. Teams, Routing & Organizations


* **Round-Robin & Collective Events**: Distribute meetings across a team or require multiple hosts together.
* **Routing Forms**: Qualify and route invitees to the right person or event type, with attribute-based routing rules.
* **Reassignment**: Auto- or manually reassign round-robin bookings.
* **Organization Hierarchy**: Parent ↔ sub-team structure, organization-wide scheduling, and centralized user management.
* **Insights & Analytics**: Org- and team-level booking analytics and reporting.


### 3.3. Automation & Workflows


* **Workflows**: Automated reminders, confirmations, and follow-ups via email and SMS.
* **Webhooks**: Trigger external systems on booking create/cancel/reschedule and other events.
* **Payments**: Collect payment at the time of booking via Stripe.
* **AI Scheduling**: Build AI agents that manage scheduling through the v2 API and the hosted MCP server, including AI phone-call event types.


### 3.4. Developer Platform & API


* **API v2 (REST)**: Manage bookings, event types, schedules, availability, slots, routing forms, teams, organizations, webhooks, and calendars. Authenticate via OAuth or API key (Bearer token; HTTPS required). Default rate limit 120 requests/minute, increasable on request.
* **Cal Atoms**: Drop-in React components — Booker, availability settings, event types, calendar connect, payment form, and more — to embed scheduling natively in your app.
* **MCP Server**: Connect AI clients to Cal.com scheduling via the Model Context Protocol at mcp.cal.com (or self-hosted).
* **App Store Framework**: Build and integrate apps spanning calendars, video, CRM, payments, and automation.
* Reference: https://cal.com/docs/api-reference/v2/introduction · Full docs index: https://cal.com/docs/llms.txt


### 3.5. Security & Compliance


* **HIPAA**: Suitable for handling PHI, with a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) available on organization/enterprise plans.
* **SOC 2, ISO 27001**: Independently audited security and information-management standards.
* **GDPR & CCPA**: Privacy compliance for EU and California data subjects.
* **Access & Identity**: SSO (SAML, OIDC), SCIM user provisioning, and granular RBAC / permission-based access control (PBAC).
* **Governance**: Organization-wide audit logs, role management, and centralized administration.


